basic summary of conversion :
1. change the sprintf function prototype to deal
    with the prototype as defined in <stdio.h>

2. add -fwritable-strings.

3. comment out the two loops in makedefs.c that
   appear in the do_objects and do_permonster (or
   names close to that) that attempt to make the
   include files upper-case.  The fwritable-strings
   doesn't include register *char's.

4. Let it run through makedefs-p, makedefs-o then
   kill it as it goes into allmain (it wil kill itself,
   but it takes too long).

5. go to the include directory and change all object and
   monster names to uppercase (I used ed - it took about
   3 minutes) and change spaces and hyphens to _.
   Change the DEFINEs back to define. 

6. go back to the src and continue with the make 
   (make sure to make backup copyies of onames.h and
    pm.h just in case it starts over at making makedefs)

7. Install as per instructions.

Let me know how it goes.

Erica.

